1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,500
Underwriting Desk begins with the deal, not a chat box.
Importing this four-file synthetic package validates

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:11,000
the declared sources in the browser before any
return conclusion appears.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
The package clears the mechanical intake,
but it cannot grade itself.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Ordinary-cohort retention is 83.6 percent against a separate
95 percent Desk policy, so further diligence is required.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Every important output retains a source path. Here,
the analyst can inspect the exact customer periods

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,000
behind retention instead of trusting a filename,
summary, or model-generated citation.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,500
A bounded scenario changes growth and immediately recomputes
terminal value and returns with deterministic math.

8
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:42,000
The interface marks it as an unapproved what-if;
the canonical package case remains unchanged.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Human judgment stays explicit. A named analyst records
a meeting observation and can assign diligence work

10
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000
without rewriting company facts, fund policy,
or the calculated books.

11
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,000
For model review, the user selects the exact evidence subset
and confirms what leaves the browser.

12
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:06,000
The hosted reviewer returns a cited counterthesis as proposed
language, never as an approved conclusion.

13
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:10,500
A named human must accept, reject, or edit that proposal.
Acceptance records the reviewer and preserves

14
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:15,000
the evidence references; it still cannot change
financial calculations or policy tests.

15
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,500
The resulting investment-committee memo combines deterministic
economics, analyst judgment, and accepted model language

16
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:24,000
with provenance. It remains a synthetic working draft,
with the IC decision explicitly pending.
